    <!-- ============ SECTION 1: WHICH SECTION ============ -->
    <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />
    <h2 id="which-section" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-12">🤔 Which Section Should You Visit?</h2>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-8">Every section is, technically, the same wall. But no two give you the same day. The differences that matter aren't the distance or the ticket price — they're <strong>how crowded it gets, how hard you have to work, and what the wall is actually doing when you get there</strong> (sweeping over ridges, dropping into a lake, or lit up against a night sky). The sections below are ordered by how likely they are to suit a first or second visit.</p>

    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">How the Six Great Wall Sections Compare</h3>

    <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8 not-prose">
      <table class="w-full text-sm text-left border-collapse bg-white rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="bg-gray-900 text-white">
            <th class="px-3 py-3 font-bold align-bottom">Section</th>
            <th class="px-3 py-3 font-bold align-bottom">Distance from Beijing</th>
